#!/usr/bin/env python3
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
"""rocq-live: live Rocq proof sessions for any project, no per-project setup.

  rocq-live goto  FILE[:LINE] [--full]  proof state just before LINE (default:
                                      end of file). Starts a session if none
                                      runs; afterwards re-checks only from the
                                      first changed character: edit, goto,
                                      repeat. With a LINE, a finished Qed proof
                                      before it that was not edited is taken as
                                      Admitted (statement checked, tactics not);
                                      --full, or no LINE, checks every proof
  rocq-live run   FILE[:LINE] 'TAC.'  run sentences on the current state (or on
                                      the state before LINE), print the goals
                                      or the error (error: no change)
  rocq-live query FILE 'CMD.'         run, print, undo (Search, Check, Print, About)
  rocq-live try   FILE 'T1.' 'T2.' ..  run each tactic alone on the current state:
                                      which work, goals left; state unchanged
  rocq-live audit FILE [NAME..] [--allow AX,..]  Admitted/admit/axioms and
                                      Print Assumptions vs the allowed axioms
  rocq-live check FILE [--allow-stale] [--rebuild] [--all-errors]  coqc's verdict on the whole
                                      file (errors in coqc's format, exit 0 OK, 1
                                      error, 2 not checked), from the live session:
                                      re-checks only what an edit can affect (a
                                      Qed proof's tactics: that proof; a statement,
                                      definition or instance: the proofs that can
                                      see it). Refuses
                                      (exit 2) if a dependency's .vo is out of date.
                                      --all-errors: every failing proof, not just
                                      the first error
  rocq-live compile FILE [--deps-only] write .vo files with the project's build
                                      step: out-of-date dependencies, then FILE
  rocq-live impact FILE               what an edit to FILE breaks elsewhere: compile
                                      FILE and every file that requires it, in order
                                      and in parallel (ROCQ_LIVE_JOBS); a failure
                                      skips what depends on it
  rocq-live back  FILE [N]            undo the last N runs (default 1)
  rocq-live goals FILE                print the current goals
  rocq-live start FILE [LINE]         like goto, but always a fresh session
  rocq-live stop  FILE | --all [--force]  stop the session(s) at once (--all
                                      spares busy ones, serving another request,
                                      unless --force)
  rocq-live list                      running sessions: memory, idle time, limits
  rocq-live gc                        apply the limits now (also automatic)
  rocq-live stats [FILE] [--since 7d] what rocq-live did and saved (local log only)
  rocq-live info  FILE                project root, toolchain and load path found
  rocq-live mcp                       serve the same commands as MCP tools (stdio)

Each session is a background process holding one `coqtop -emacs` for one file,
so a step costs only that step: no prefix replays.

Project detection (from FILE's directory upwards, nearest marker wins):
  .rocq-live     optional config, `key value` lines (see below)
  dune-project   load path from `dune coq top` (also builds what FILE imports)
  _CoqProject    load path from its -Q/-R/-I/-arg lines (build it yourself)
Toolchain: the config's `switch`, else $ROCQ_LIVE_SWITCH, else the current opam
switch if it has coqtop, else coqtop on PATH.

.rocq-live keys (all optional; relative paths are from its directory):
  switch   rocq-9.0               opam switch (`path`: use coqtop on PATH)
  flags    -Q theories My         load path flags, verbatim
  loadpath scripts/loadpath.sh {file}   command printing the flags; may build
  build    make -j8 vos           command run before each start/goto
  compile  make {vo}              how `compile` builds one file ({file}: the .v,
                                  {vo}: its .vo relative to the root); default:
                                  coqc with the load path, or dune build
  axioms   classic functional_extensionality_dep   axioms `audit` accepts

Limits (machine-wide; environment, else ~/.config/rocq-live/config with the
same `key value` lines; read at each use, so changes apply to running sessions):
  max_mb       ROCQ_LIVE_MAX_MB       all sessions together (default: half the RAM)
  session_mb   ROCQ_LIVE_SESSION_MB   one session (default: max_mb)
  max_sessions ROCQ_LIVE_MAX_SESSIONS (default 16)
  grace        ROCQ_LIVE_GRACE        a session used this recently (seconds) is
                                      not stopped for max_sessions (default 600)
  idle         ROCQ_LIVE_IDLE         seconds before an idle session exits (1200;
                                      its recipe restores it on next use)
Over max_mb, or over max_sessions (sparing sessions used within `grace`), the
least recently used idle sessions are stopped (GC: when a session starts, after
each request, and every second while a step runs). A step that takes a session over session_mb, or the total over
max_mb with nothing idle left to stop, is interrupted, and that session's
coqtop is restarted to give the memory back. A busy session is never stopped.
Environment: ROCQ_LIVE_FLAGS (load path override), ROCQ_LIVE_SWITCH,
ROCQ_LIVE_TIMEOUT (seconds per step; default 600 for goto/start, 120 others),
ROCQ_LIVE_TRY_TIMEOUT (seconds per tactic in `try`; default 30),
ROCQ_LIVE_FAST=0 (goto checks every proof, as --full),
ROCQ_LIVE_REUSE=0 (after an edit inside a proof, re-run every proof after it),
ROCQ_LIVE_COMPACT=0 (run/try show every hypothesis, not only the changed ones),
ROCQ_LIVE_STATS=0 (record nothing in ~/.cache/rocq-live/stats.jsonl),
ROCQ_LIVE_DAEMON=0 (no background process: each call starts coqtop, rebuilds
the state from the recipe and exits; slower per call, nothing left running).

Recipes: each session saves its last goto line and the runs on top of it in
~/.cache/rocq-live/recipes (kept 7 days). A session stopped by gc, the idle
timeout or a reboot is restored from it on its next use (fast replay), and
says so; `stop` forgets it.

A running session watches the .vo/.vos files of the project modules it has
loaded; when one is rebuilt, the session restarts coqtop and replays the file
to the last goto line and the runs on top, and says so. `goto` also rebuilds
FILE's imports first (dune, or the `build`/`loadpath` command), so: edit an
imported file, then goto, and the new version is used.
"""
